              "id": "3206dd5e-115e-3f19-ad1e-f06168d1e1ab",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Prohibited C Function Found\" is a vulnerability that arises when a C++ program uses a function that is considered unsafe due to its potential to cause buffer overflows, format string vulnerabilities, or other types of security issues. In this case, the function `std::getenv` is used, which can lead to security vulnerabilities as it returns a pointer to a string that represents the value of the environment variable. This string can be modified by another process, leading to potential race conditions.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to avoid using `std::getenv` and instead use a safer alternative that does not have the same potential for race conditions or other security issues. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nA safer alternative to `std::getenv` is to use `std::getenv_s`, which is a more secure version of `std::getenv`. Here is how you can modify the code:\n\n```cpp\nsize_t requiredSize;\nchar* buffer;\n\n// Get the required buffer size\ngetenv_s(&requiredSize, NULL, 0, \"HIPSOLVER_TEST_DATA\");\n\nif (requiredSize == 0)\n{\n    printf(\"HIPSOLVER_TEST_DATA doesn't exist!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n}\n\n// Allocate memory for the buffer\nbuffer = (char*) malloc(requiredSize * sizeof(char));\n\n// Retrieve the value of the environment variable\ngetenv_s(&requiredSize, buffer, requiredSize, \"HIPSOLVER_TEST_DATA\");\n\ndatadir = buffer;\n\nfree(buffer);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `<cstdlib>`: for `std::getenv` and `std::getenv_s`\n- `<cstdio>`: for `printf`\n- `<cstring>`: for `strlen`\n\n## OWASP and CWE Links\n\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS154189"
                ]
              }
